    new "No pasa nada, no pienses más en ello. Dejemos el asunto así. Por favor, sigue participando."

    old "Place the crown on your own head"
    new "Coloca la corona sobre tu propia cabeza"

    old "Suddenly, Sarah's hands steadied. The tremblings of her fingers faded."
    new "De repente, las manos de Sarah se estabilizaron. Los temblores de sus dedos se desvanecieron."

    old "She was the daughter of a long line."
    new "Ella era la hija de una larga estirpe."

    old "She was no slave."
    new "Ella no era una esclava."

    old "She would play no part in this farce."
    new "Ella no participaría en esta farsa."

    old "Sarah turned to face the crowd."
    new "Sarah se giró para encarar a la multitud."

    old "Deathly silence."
    new "Silencio mortal."

    old "She raised up the crown and placed it atop her own head."
    new "Ella levantó la corona y se la colocó en la cabeza."

    old "A shock ran through the crowd."
    new "Una oleada de conmoción recorrió a la multitud."

    old "Then screaming. Insults. Rage."
    new "Entonces, gritos. Insultos. Furia."

    old "Sarah never saw the blade that ended her life; the world only went dark."
    new "Sarah nunca vio la hoja que le acabó con la vida; el mundo simplemente se oscureció."

    old "They had made her a slave."
    new "La habían convertido en esclava."

    old "But she died a Princess."
    new "Pero murió como una princesa."

    old "Sarah was rushed back to her seat by Jaeid."
    new "Jaeid la llevó apresuradamente de vuelta a su asiento."

    old "The tears still streamed down her face."
    new "Las lágrimas seguían corriendo por su rostro."

    old "She clamped onto him."
    new "Se aferró a él."

    old "She repeated the words like a mantra."
    new "Repitió las palabras como un mantra."

    old "Do not worry, Sarah."
    new "No te preocupes, Sarah."

    old "Thank you, thank you."
    new "Gracias, gracias."

    old "She kept repeating the words, over and over again."
    new "Ella seguía repitiendo las palabras, una y otra vez."

    old "She felt Jaeid wrap his strong arms around her, pulling her into an embrace."
    new "Sintió que Jaeid la rodeaba con sus fuertes brazos, atrayéndola hacia un abrazo."

    old "And she wept."
    new "Y lloró."

    old "She held back nothing from him anymore as she cried into his chest."
    new "Ya no le ocultaba nada mientras lloraba contra su pecho."

    old "Everything she had endured over these weeks came out from her eyes."
    new "Todo lo que había soportado durante esas semanas brotó de sus ojos."

    old "And the man who had kept her safe for all of it, only held her in comfort."
    new "Y el hombre que la había mantenido a salvo durante todo aquello solo la abrazó para consolarla."

    old "Around her, the room and the festivities faded into nothing."
    new "A su alrededor, la habitación y las festividades se desvanecieron en la nada."

    old "Only herself and Jaeid remained."
    new "Solo ella y Jaeid permanecían."

    old "Sarah didn't remember much of the rest of the night."
    new "Sarah no recordaba mucho del resto de la noche."

    old "She only came back to her senses when they returned home. As much as this could ever be a home."
    new "Ella solo volvió en sí cuando regresaron a casa. Por mucho que aquello pudiera llegar a ser un hogar."

    old "Jaeid stood in the dark, lit only by the moonlight."
    new "Jaeid estaba de pie en la oscuridad, iluminado únicamente por la luz de la luna."

    old "You saved me..."
    new "Me salvaste..."

    old "I did no such thing."
    new "Yo no hice tal cosa."

    old "You did...he was going to give me to that man and you..."
    new "Tú... él iba a entregarme a ese hombre, y tú..."

    old "I protected you. I did only the duty that is demanded of a man."
    new "Te protegí. Solo cumplí con el deber que se exige a un hombre."

    old "But the Khan...his anger...what if..."
    new "Pero el kan... su ira... ¿y si...?"

    old "What if he harmed me?"
    new "¿Y si me hubiera hecho daño?"

    old "Gladly that I suffer a thousand deaths in glory, than live one lifetime in shame."
    new "Prefiero mil muertes gloriosas a una vida entera en la vergüenza."

    old "Sarah threw her arms around him and kept him in an embrace."
    new "Sarah lo abrazó con fuerza y no lo soltó."

    old "Sleep with Jaeid"
    new "Dormir con Jaeid"

    old "Holding him in her embrace, Sarah hugged him tighter and tighter."
    new "Mientras lo mantenía en su abrazo, Sarah lo apretó cada vez con más fuerza."

    old "Safety."
    new "Seguridad."

    old "In his arms, so close to him, she had felt for the first time in a long time...safe."
    new "En sus brazos, tan cerca de él, por primera vez en mucho tiempo se sintió... a salvo."

    old "She didn't want it to stop. Not ever."
    new "Ella no quería que eso terminara. Nunca."

    old "Her hands wandered naturally across his strong body."
    new "Sus manos recorrieron con naturalidad el cuerpo fuerte de él."

    old "As if the touching of each fingertip might cause her to possess him for a moment longer."
    new "Como si el roce de cada yema de sus dedos pudiera hacer que ella lo poseyera por un instante más."

    old "Sarah pulled up his shirt and pressed her lips up against his exposed chest."
    new "Sarah le levantó la camisa y presionó sus labios contra su pecho descubierto."

